            p("Every ward could phone a central desk for each number, which is slow. Wards could pick numbers at random from a huge range, which works but makes the files hard to keep in order. Or each number could start with the date and time, then the ward, then a counter: unique, and sorted by birth time."),
            analogy("<strong>Hospital wristbands.</strong> The central desk is the ticket server, the random numbers are UUIDs, and time plus ward plus counter is a Snowflake id."),
